{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8, hours 06:00-14:00 America/Chicago) says his warehouse office desktop BL-DT-0108 won't connect to the network. His shift starts in about an hour, and he can't work until it's fixed. Checked: account is active, not locked, sign-in not blocked. Device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro desktop) shows OFFLINE. Last check-in was 2026-10-11 01:21 UTC. Disk is fine (78% free), no warnings. Found: the device has no path to the network. The KB only covers laptop Wi-Fi (KB-014), not a wired desktop with no network. It could be the cable, switch port, NIC, or a wider warehouse network outage. We don't know yet whether others in the warehouse office are affected. I've asked the user to reseat the cable, restart the PC, and tell us whether colleagues are affected. Still needed: on-site or remote check of the network drop, switch port, and NIC. If several warehouse users are down, raise the priority.",
  "reason": "Desktop offline, no KB covers wired desktop connectivity, user blocked with imminent shift"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked and our system shows your warehouse desktop has been offline since earlier tonight. I've passed this to our Tier 2 network team and told them your shift starts soon. While you wait, a few quick things to try: 1) Check that the network cable is plugged in firmly at the back of the PC and at the wall. Unplug it and plug it back in. 2) Restart the PC. 3) Let us know if anyone else nearby in the warehouse office has lost network too. That tells us whether the problem is your PC or the building's network. If it comes back online, please reply and tell us. Otherwise Tier 2 will follow up with you.",
  "internal_note": "User was looked up: active account, no lockouts. Device BL-DT-0108 (desktop) is offline. Last check-in was 2026-10-11 01:21 UTC. Disk is fine, no warnings. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network (KB-014 is only for laptop Wi-Fi), so per process I escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) as P2, user blocked, shift starting in about 1 hour. I gave the user basic steps (reseat cable, restart) and asked whether colleagues are affected. If several warehouse users are down, raise to P1/P2 as a site outage.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
